1
00:01:33,310 --> 00:01:37,390
[Manager: Found a sketch of a flower you did]

2
00:01:37,390 --> 00:01:39,380
Sakura. Breakfast is ready.
[Should I mail it over to Singapore?]

3
00:01:39,380 --> 00:01:41,180
Coming.

4
00:01:43,930 --> 00:01:46,380
I thought it was my turn to cook today.

5
00:01:46,380 --> 00:01:49,150
You get a break
for your first week living abroad.

6
00:01:49,150 --> 00:01:50,850
Who made that rule?

7
00:01:50,850 --> 00:01:52,700
Me. Just now.

8
00:01:52,700 --> 00:01:54,790
I wasn't informed.

9
00:01:54,790 --> 00:01:57,550
If you've got objections, I'll hear you out.

10
00:01:59,530 --> 00:02:02,240
- Thanks for breakfast.
- You're welcome.

11
00:02:02,240 --> 00:02:05,730
First, we'll visit Merlion Park.
Then, Mandai.

12
00:02:05,730 --> 00:02:09,600
Afterwards we'll take a river cruise,
to close out the day in Marina Bay.

13
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:13,720
What about here?

14
00:02:13,720 --> 00:02:15,080
Katong?

15
00:02:16,030 --> 00:02:18,000
Maybe not today.

16
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:20,950
I want to make sure we catch
the nighttime fountain show.

17
00:02:24,350 --> 00:02:27,210
You still haven't shared
your location with me.

18
00:02:27,210 --> 00:02:29,160
I haven't.

19
00:02:29,160 --> 00:02:32,530
We're overseas. What if there's an emergency?

20
00:02:33,370 --> 00:02:35,700
You don't need to worry so much.

21
00:02:35,700 --> 00:02:38,220
I'm not a kid who's going to get lost.

22
00:02:38,220 --> 00:02:42,200
I know. But I feel better
knowing I can come find you.

23
00:02:53,940 --> 00:02:55,450
Smile!

24
00:02:58,600 --> 00:03:03,100
We're lucky to have
another Japanese guide join us.

25
00:03:03,100 --> 00:03:05,000
I look forward to working with you tomorrow.

26
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:07,090
Likewise.

27
00:03:07,090 --> 00:03:11,740
Today, I want you to enjoy yourself,
so you're ready to entertain our guests.

28
00:03:11,740 --> 00:03:12,650
Yes, ma'am.

29
00:03:12,650 --> 00:03:15,790
If you're able to guide him around,
you'll be set to go.

30
00:03:15,790 --> 00:03:18,280
I'm a tough customer to please.

31
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:20,730
I know.

32
00:03:33,760 --> 00:03:36,920
- Wow!
- Woah!

33
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:54,180
Landscapes, portraits,
and then your newest works in the back.

34
00:03:56,480 --> 00:03:59,360
[MANDAI x LUN]

35
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:04,300
Who is this?

36
00:04:04,300 --> 00:04:06,370
Do you know who she is?

37
00:04:13,420 --> 00:04:15,910
That's not an answer.

38
00:04:15,910 --> 00:04:17,720
I don't know.

39
00:04:17,720 --> 00:04:20,160
I felt a sudden urge
to draw this woman yesterday.

40
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:22,140
My pencil wouldn't stop moving.

41
00:04:22,830 --> 00:04:24,540
Did you eat?

42
00:04:25,410 --> 00:04:27,230
A bit.

43
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:31,640
Should I go get something for you?

44
00:04:33,400 --> 00:04:34,830
It's fine.

45
00:04:36,260 --> 00:04:39,840
I'm going to take a walk to clear my head.

46
00:04:50,100 --> 00:04:52,560
Yum!

47
00:04:57,110 --> 00:05:00,460
[Will you marry me?]

48
00:05:02,500 --> 00:05:04,580
This is so good.

49
00:05:10,260 --> 00:05:11,550
Sakura.

50
00:05:11,550 --> 00:05:12,920
Yeah?

51
00:05:18,780 --> 00:05:21,060
- Sorry.
- It's fine.

52
00:05:22,860 --> 00:05:25,490
Natsume, your timing is awful.

53
00:05:25,490 --> 00:05:27,360
Sorry to bother on your day off.

54
00:05:27,360 --> 00:05:29,590
We're discussing
the Katong renovations today.

55
00:05:29,590 --> 00:05:31,510
Katong?

56
00:05:31,510 --> 00:05:32,920
Does it have to be today?

57
00:05:32,920 --> 00:05:35,830
<i>It's the only day
we could schedule a meeting.</i>

58
00:05:35,830 --> 00:05:37,680
Alright.

59
00:05:37,680 --> 00:05:39,420
I'll be right there.

60
00:05:44,210 --> 00:05:48,230
Katong... is that the place
I asked about this morning?

61
00:05:48,230 --> 00:05:49,620
Yeah.

62
00:05:49,620 --> 00:05:51,600
I'd like to go there.

63
00:05:52,200 --> 00:05:54,680
It seemed like an interesting place.

64
00:05:55,840 --> 00:05:57,400
Sure.

65
00:06:02,120 --> 00:06:03,960
Stay on the main roads, okay?

66
00:06:03,960 --> 00:06:07,690
The back alleys are harder to navigate.

67
00:06:07,690 --> 00:06:10,520
When you're done, wait at a cafe.
I'll come get you.

68
00:06:10,520 --> 00:06:13,280
You don't need to worry, I'll be fine.

69
00:06:13,280 --> 00:06:16,830
I know. But I want to, okay?

70
00:06:17,700 --> 00:06:19,970
Call or text me if anything crops up.

71
00:06:19,970 --> 00:06:22,220
- You too, Eita.
- Yeah.

72
00:06:34,750 --> 00:06:38,050
[Eita]

73
00:08:01,410 --> 00:08:03,430
What just happened?

74
00:08:07,840 --> 00:08:11,560
Alright next up, Katong.
How's the progress for this one?

75
00:08:16,100 --> 00:08:18,860
This neighborhood in particular
has a lot of old historic...

76
00:08:18,860 --> 00:08:22,560
Ownership of property here
gets a bit complicated.

77
00:08:22,560 --> 00:08:25,230
Are you listening?

78
00:08:25,230 --> 00:08:28,210
Yeah. Sorry.

79
00:08:28,210 --> 00:08:32,790
Yeah, that is true. The buildings are
certainly colorful on Instagram.

80
00:08:32,790 --> 00:08:36,580
It'd be cool if it can kind of go viral.

81
00:09:22,440 --> 00:09:25,670
[Eita: It's pouring outside]
[Should I come get you now?]

82
00:09:25,670 --> 00:09:29,030
Don't worry, it'll let up soon.
[Don't worry, it'll let up soon]

83
00:09:30,350 --> 00:09:35,180
You can speak Japanese?

84
00:09:35,180 --> 00:09:38,380
No. I don't speak Japanese.

85
00:09:38,380 --> 00:09:40,160
But you just...

86
00:09:40,160 --> 00:09:44,390
Right. I shouldn't know Japanese.

87
00:09:44,970 --> 00:09:46,610
I think?

88
00:09:46,610 --> 00:09:48,170
You think?

89
00:09:50,870 --> 00:09:53,310
That's strange, right?

90
00:09:57,480 --> 00:09:59,700
It rains suddenly here.

91
00:10:01,120 --> 00:10:02,970
I like that.

92
00:10:04,180 --> 00:10:05,820
The squall?

93
00:10:06,730 --> 00:10:08,720
No warning.

94
00:10:10,330 --> 00:10:12,670
You're a strange one, huh?

95
00:10:12,670 --> 00:10:14,440
As are you.

96
00:10:17,260 --> 00:10:19,210
Do you draw?

97
00:10:20,780 --> 00:10:22,810
Sometimes.

98
00:10:22,810 --> 00:10:24,200
Can I see?

99
00:10:24,200 --> 00:10:25,980
I used to draw.

100
00:10:25,980 --> 00:10:27,620
How about now?

101
00:10:27,620 --> 00:10:31,140
I stopped somehow.

102
00:10:31,140 --> 00:10:33,490
Somehow.

103
00:10:33,490 --> 00:10:35,010
Yes.

104
00:10:37,090 --> 00:10:38,540
That's a shame.

105
00:10:38,540 --> 00:10:40,840
Would've loved to see your drawings.

106
00:10:55,960 --> 00:10:58,430
- I'm sorry!
- It's okay.

107
00:11:05,230 --> 00:11:09,200
Goodness, your wonderful sketches are ruined.

108
00:11:11,290 --> 00:11:13,230
Always the rain, isn't it?

109
00:11:16,350 --> 00:11:18,010
Come in.

110
00:11:18,010 --> 00:11:19,630
Come in!

111
00:11:37,830 --> 00:11:39,720
Please, have a seat wherever.

112
00:11:39,720 --> 00:11:41,080
Thank you.

113
00:11:44,460 --> 00:11:46,420
I know this place.

114
00:11:47,910 --> 00:11:50,020
Have I come here before?

115
00:12:12,710 --> 00:12:15,500
I feel like we've met before.

116
00:12:15,500 --> 00:12:16,910
Huh?

117
00:12:16,910 --> 00:12:18,350
Sorry.

118
00:12:19,840 --> 00:12:22,940
I feel like we've met before.

119
00:12:26,250 --> 00:12:29,000
Sorry. Nothing.

120
00:12:42,070 --> 00:12:43,420
Thank you.

121
00:12:44,830 --> 00:12:48,550
Have the two of us dined here before?

122
00:12:51,600 --> 00:12:52,870
Who knows?

123
00:12:52,870 --> 00:12:57,950
I can't remember every customer who visits.
Not at my age.

124
00:13:11,180 --> 00:13:14,130
I know this flavor.

125
00:13:14,130 --> 00:13:16,010
This tastes nostalgic.

126
00:13:30,490 --> 00:13:32,550
- Sakura.
- Lun.

127
00:13:35,540 --> 00:13:37,940
How do you know my name?

128
00:13:37,940 --> 00:13:40,040
How do you know mine?

129
00:13:46,180 --> 00:13:49,130
Wei? What brings you here?

130
00:13:51,830 --> 00:13:55,200
You're back, Sakura.

131
00:13:57,670 --> 00:14:00,080
You know her?

132
00:14:03,270 --> 00:14:04,940
What do you want now?

133
00:14:04,940 --> 00:14:06,680
Huh?

134
00:14:06,680 --> 00:14:10,920
Hold on. She may have something to do with
my accident four years ago.

135
00:14:15,950 --> 00:14:17,790
We're leaving.

136
00:14:20,770 --> 00:14:23,100
You know her, don't you?

137
00:14:23,100 --> 00:14:26,200
I don't.

138
00:14:26,200 --> 00:14:30,240
- How am I related to her?
- Enough!

139
00:14:30,240 --> 00:14:32,950
What's all the fuss?

140
00:14:37,890 --> 00:14:39,880
Pardon us, ma'am.

141
00:14:39,880 --> 00:14:42,400
We'll be out of here in a moment.

142
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:44,510
Let's go.

143
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:56,580
Please.

144
00:15:10,880 --> 00:15:12,440
Lun.

145
00:15:14,910 --> 00:15:16,640
Lun.

146
00:15:17,790 --> 00:15:19,210
We're leaving.

147
00:15:35,580 --> 00:15:36,990
Lun...

148
00:15:41,880 --> 00:15:43,800
His sketchbook...

149
00:15:50,310 --> 00:15:53,000
If it's something important,

150
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:55,040
he'll come back for it, right?

151
00:15:56,190 --> 00:16:00,090
May I deliver that to him?

152
00:16:03,310 --> 00:16:06,760
May I deliver that sketchbook to him?

153
00:16:08,100 --> 00:16:09,850
Why you?

154
00:16:10,960 --> 00:16:13,020
I don't know.

155
00:16:13,020 --> 00:16:17,040
I just want to.

156
00:16:33,150 --> 00:16:39,600
[Rumah Kim Choo]

157
00:16:41,390 --> 00:16:43,070
Sakura?

158
00:16:43,070 --> 00:16:44,560
Eita.

159
00:16:44,560 --> 00:16:46,080
You okay?

160
00:16:46,800 --> 00:16:48,180
Yeah.

161
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:51,780
Where'd you get that?

162
00:16:52,740 --> 00:16:54,860
A store owner gave it to me.

163
00:16:54,860 --> 00:16:58,440
Gave it to you? Why?

164
00:16:58,440 --> 00:17:04,820
Eita, have I been to Singapore before?

165
00:17:05,580 --> 00:17:07,380
Not as far as I'm aware.

166
00:17:08,030 --> 00:17:09,980
Why?

167
00:17:09,980 --> 00:17:13,740
Everything just seems so... familiar.

168
00:17:13,740 --> 00:17:18,070
You can still feel nostalgic
about places you've never been to before.

169
00:17:18,070 --> 00:17:19,810
I guess.

170
00:17:39,450 --> 00:17:42,260
Wow!

171
00:17:42,260 --> 00:17:44,500
The city lights are beautiful!

172
00:17:44,500 --> 00:17:45,960
Aren't they?

173
00:17:54,540 --> 00:17:57,400
Look, it's glowing up there!

174
00:17:57,400 --> 00:17:58,740
You're right.

175
00:17:58,740 --> 00:18:00,780
Wow...

176
00:18:22,150 --> 00:18:23,920
Sakura.

177
00:18:23,920 --> 00:18:25,240
Yeah?

178
00:18:27,880 --> 00:18:30,930
- I...
- What was that?

179
00:18:32,930 --> 00:18:36,410
- I love you!
- Stop it, you're embarrassing me!

180
00:18:40,280 --> 00:18:43,080
I had planned to ask

181
00:18:43,080 --> 00:18:46,020
once we settled in a bit more, but...

182
00:18:47,250 --> 00:18:48,730
Yeah?

183
00:19:00,780 --> 00:19:02,840
Will you marry me?

184
00:19:32,370 --> 00:19:33,570
Sakura?

185
00:19:33,570 --> 00:19:35,070
Sakura?

186
00:19:35,740 --> 00:19:37,070
Sakura!

187
00:19:53,760 --> 00:19:56,860
You're okay. What a relief.

188
00:19:56,860 --> 00:19:58,680
I...

189
00:20:00,420 --> 00:20:01,810
Here.

190
00:20:01,810 --> 00:20:03,860
Thanks.

191
00:20:03,860 --> 00:20:08,420
You must have been tired.
Rest up for tomorrow.

192
00:20:08,420 --> 00:20:10,660
Thanks.

193
00:20:10,660 --> 00:20:12,500
I have to call your mother.

194
00:20:12,500 --> 00:20:15,800
I promised I'd tell her when you woke up.

195
00:20:15,800 --> 00:20:17,670
You contacted her?

196
00:20:17,670 --> 00:20:22,310
Of course I did. I whisked away
her only daughter to foreign lands.

197
00:20:22,310 --> 00:20:24,210
You didn't have to.

198
00:20:24,210 --> 00:20:26,440
Don't say that.

199
00:20:47,650 --> 00:20:49,320
Sakura.

200
00:21:22,720 --> 00:21:24,520
What're you doing?

201
00:21:26,130 --> 00:21:29,640
I think I can finally complete my sketch.

202
00:22:12,060 --> 00:22:14,010
203...

203
00:22:26,850 --> 00:22:28,570
Sakura!
